  "preamble": "Schwa [ə] surfaces as, or historically becomes, the open-mid front vowel [ɛ]. In French the e muet of open syllables alternates with [ɛ] in closed syllables within verb paradigms, and in Delhi Hindustani /ə/ is realized as [ɛ] around /ɦ/.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Fronting, Lowering, Closed-Syllable Alternation",
